{"name":"Mandarin Red","hex":"#e84f3c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mandarin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A high government bureaucrat of the Chinese Empire. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A pedantic or elitist bureaucrat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to or reminiscent of mandarins; deliberately superior or complex; esoteric, highbrow, obscurantist."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mandarin"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mandarin (character)","blocks":[{"text":"The Mandarin is a supervillain appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. He is the archenemy of Iron Man. The character was created by Stan Lee and designed by Don Heck, first appearing in Tales of Suspense #50. The character is described as being born in China before the Communist revolution to a wealthy Chinese father and an English aristocratic mother, both of whom died when he was young. He is characterized as a megalomaniac, attempting to conquer the world on several occasions, yet also possessing a strong sense of honor. The Mandarin is portrayed as a genius scientist and a skilled martial artist. However, his primary sources of power are 10 rings that he adapted from the alien technology of a crashed spaceship. Each ring has a different power and is worn on a specific finger. Though his primary obsession is Iron Man, given his high status as a supervillain, he has also come into conflict with Thor, Hulk, Shang-Chi, and other superheroes in the Marvel Universe."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/ca/Mandarin_%28Marvel_Comics_character_circa_2011%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mandarin_(character)","wikidata":"Q2417914"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e9/Tales_of_Suspense_%281959%29_-50.png/250px-Tales_of_Suspense_%281959%29_-50.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e9/Tales_of_Suspense_%281959%29_-50.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e9/Tales_of_Suspense_%281959%29_-50.png/250px-Tales_of_Suspense_%281959%29_-50.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The cover of Tales of Suspense #50 (Feb. 1964), the first appearance of the Mandarin, art by Jack Kirby","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATales_of_Suspense_(1959)_-50.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Ben_Kingsley_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg/500px-Ben_Kingsley_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Ben_Kingsley_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg/1280px-Ben_Kingsley_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Ben_Kingsley_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg/500px-Ben_Kingsley_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ben Kingsley at the 2014 San Diego Comic-Con","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABen_Kingsley_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Tony_Leung_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Tony_Leung_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/37/Tony_Leung_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Tony_Leung_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Tony_Leung_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tony Leung in 2016","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATony_Leung_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Cardinal.jpg/500px-Cardinal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Cardinal.jpg/500px-Cardinal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACardinal.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Cardinal_Th%C3%A9odore_Adrien_Sarr_2.JPG/500px-Cardinal_Th%C3%A9odore_Adrien_Sarr_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&